    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with an elite 74.11 efficiency score, buoyed by a prime matchup against Ure\u00f1a\u2019s high xERA of 4.73. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused leadoff and high-order anchors: **Corbin Carroll** (68.93) and **James Wood** (64.68) are must-starts. Despite facing lefties, both maintain high scores because their positional utility and elite xwOBA ratings outweigh the platoon-adjusted risk. **Josh Naylor** (65.29) rounds out our top-tier plays, as his clean-up role against the shaky Schultz (5.41 xERA) provides a significant run-production floor. **Vinnie Pasquantino** also benefits from a favorable slotting, with his #3 position and platoon advantage yielding a strong 62.80 score, effectively neutralizing the talent of Gray.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (51.85). He was the clear final cut, ultimately passed over because his ceiling was capped by a tougher matchup against Meyer compared to the higher-floor opportunities afforded to **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**. While **Carson Williams** (41.82) remained in the conversation, the combination of his lower order positioning and a sub-optimal park factor kept him below our starting threshold. We continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** on the IL; until he returns, we are forced to rely on the depth of our utility bench to cover for the missing elite speed production.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the risks inherent in today's lineup. **Brice Turang** and **Kyle Karros** are facing elite hold pitchers, which creates a drag on their stolen base potential; specifically, the 40-60% hold rates of Imanaga and Gore are suppressing their overall output. **Gabriel Moreno** remains a \"marginal\" play at 54.85, largely due to the defensive skill of the opposing catcher, while **Seiya Suzuki** sits just inside the \"Strong\" start tier. We will be watching the weather reports closely, as any wind shifts could further impact the viability of **Henry Bolte**, whose 56.08 score is already hovering near the mid-range of our expectations.",
